<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25822" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lāŏdĭcē</span></b> ,
			ēs, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λαοδίκη</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A daughter of Priam, who married Helicāon,
				son of the Thracian king, Antenor</i>, <i><span class="en">Hyg. Fab.
				80</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A woman</i>, otherwise unknown, <i><span class="en">Ov. H. 19,
				135</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>The wife of Antiochus</i>, <i><span class="en">Val. Max.
				9, 14, 1</span></i>
			<i>ext</i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>